1
00:00:02,035 --> 00:00:03,570
(All people, organizations, businesses,
events, and places shown are fictional.)

2
00:00:03,570 --> 00:00:05,005
(Child actors filmed in a safe space
with their guardians present.)

3
00:00:11,378 --> 00:00:12,312
(Nobody but Ian Kim)

4
00:00:17,291 --> 00:00:18,659
Hold on

5
00:00:19,660 --> 00:00:22,663
I have something to say

6
00:00:23,965 --> 00:00:27,602
I think I have to tell you today

7
00:00:27,635 --> 00:00:28,970
It's silly

8
00:00:29,770 --> 00:00:33,541
It's embarassing but I've got to say it

9
00:00:34,542 --> 00:00:36,511
The truth is

10
00:00:37,111 --> 00:00:40,448
From the day we met

11
00:00:41,449 --> 00:00:44,986
I've grown braver every day

12
00:00:45,052 --> 00:00:46,439
It's true

13
00:00:50,394 --> 00:00:51,528
Why isn't Dad here yet?

14
00:00:51,862 --> 00:00:54,198
Are you waiting for Dad,
or for the chicken?

15
00:00:55,332 --> 00:00:58,202
I'm waiting for Dad,
who is bringing the chicken.

16
00:01:02,873 --> 00:01:06,210
Hey, it's Dad! Dad!

17
00:01:06,210 --> 00:01:07,411
Chicken, chicken!

18
00:01:08,378 --> 00:01:10,180
Looks so good! Cheers!

19
00:01:10,180 --> 00:01:11,215
- No, eat.
- Come on.

20
00:01:14,852 --> 00:01:16,420
(You think Half Moon is your pet?)

21
00:01:20,124 --> 00:01:22,693
- It's absolutely amazing.
- You really like it?

22
00:01:23,494 --> 00:01:24,528
I love it.

23
00:01:30,467 --> 00:01:31,935
Such a good song, isn't it?

24
00:01:35,072 --> 00:01:36,039
Are you crying?

25
00:01:40,978 --> 00:01:42,880
I was reminded of the days...

26
00:01:43,180 --> 00:01:46,316
when the song first came out and
I loved it without a care in the world.

27
00:01:47,303 --> 00:01:49,405
Because there's no going back now.

28
00:01:49,442 --> 00:01:51,310
Shall we run?

29
00:01:51,310 --> 00:01:53,713
Or shall we fly?

30
00:01:53,813 --> 00:01:56,649
Let's go hand in hand

31
00:01:57,450 --> 00:01:59,018
Let's take a slow walk

32
00:02:00,486 --> 00:02:05,624
At the time, I didn't know exactly
what she meant by those "days."

33
00:02:06,559 --> 00:02:10,463
I found myself wanting to take her
back to those "days" again.

34
00:02:14,681 --> 00:02:16,883
Look around you from time to time

35
00:02:16,883 --> 00:02:18,985
You'll never be alone

36
00:02:18,985 --> 00:02:21,454
You'll see that I'm by your side

37
00:02:21,454 --> 00:02:23,857
Wherever you are

38
00:02:23,857 --> 00:02:25,992
I'll always remember

39
00:02:26,059 --> 00:02:28,929
The vast waves

40
00:02:30,463 --> 00:02:33,166
That carry your dreams

41
00:02:39,056 --> 00:02:43,761
(The one and only voice that lights you up
in the deepest night.)

42
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:51,135
Thank you for bringing me.

43
00:02:51,802 --> 00:02:54,672
You let me have what I love,
so I thought I should help you too.

44
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:58,509
I feel good, like I finally did
something for you too.

45
00:03:00,678 --> 00:03:03,781
If you're free, I'll buy you dinner.

46
00:03:03,781 --> 00:03:04,748
What do you want to eat?

47
00:03:05,349 --> 00:03:06,917
Well, what should we eat?

48
00:03:08,326 --> 00:03:11,822
Over dinner, I'd love to talk about
Book 3 and the concert the whole time.

49
00:03:16,827 --> 00:03:17,795
Let's go.

50
00:03:19,463 --> 00:03:21,365
Are you two on a date?

51
00:03:23,234 --> 00:03:24,268
Chef!

52
00:03:25,436 --> 00:03:26,670
It's not like that.

53
00:03:27,171 --> 00:03:30,341
Then should you be grabbing
her hand like that?

54
00:03:31,108 --> 00:03:33,410
- Who is this?
- This is…

55
00:03:37,147 --> 00:03:39,081
Perhaps it's thanks to you,
Mr. Tak Mu I.

56
00:03:39,105 --> 00:03:40,784
There are a lot of eyes on us.

57
00:03:47,324 --> 00:03:49,527
While we're at it, it's nice to meet you.

58
00:03:49,552 --> 00:03:52,530
I'm Kang Hee Su, the owner-chef of the
restaurant where Yu Il will be working.

59
00:03:56,700 --> 00:03:59,570
Sounds like you already know me,
so I'll skip the introduction.

60
00:04:05,209 --> 00:04:06,343
Hey, Yu Il.

61
00:04:06,510 --> 00:04:09,346
I was just thinking of calling you,
and we ran into each other here.

62
00:04:09,613 --> 00:04:10,648
I know, right?

63
00:04:10,648 --> 00:04:12,650
Chef, do you like Ian Kim too?

64
00:04:13,017 --> 00:04:15,152
No, Ryu Min told me to come.

65
00:04:17,033 --> 00:04:18,923
You know Ryu Min?

66
00:04:19,590 --> 00:04:23,861
Min's in that green room over there,
so you can go say hello.

67
00:04:24,728 --> 00:04:26,564
We're hungry, so we'll be going.

68
00:04:28,032 --> 00:04:30,301
Then I'll see you at work.

69
00:04:30,768 --> 00:04:33,771
By the way, have you decided where to go?

70
00:04:35,172 --> 00:04:39,510
It's late now, so most places
around here must already be closed.

71
00:04:40,326 --> 00:04:43,247
Instead of going to another place,
why don't you try The Kitchen?

72
00:04:44,315 --> 00:04:45,549
Your restaurant, Chef?

73
00:04:45,983 --> 00:04:48,285
I was going to take Ryu Min there
to feed him anyway.

74
00:04:55,726 --> 00:04:56,727
Mr. Tak.

75
00:04:57,595 --> 00:05:01,398
Do you think people won't recognize you
with a mask and a hat on?

76
00:05:02,533 --> 00:05:04,835
It seems you don't care about
how uncomfortable...

77
00:05:05,669 --> 00:05:08,038
someone may feel when you grab her hand...

78
00:05:08,772 --> 00:05:10,107
without thinking.

79
00:05:17,715 --> 00:05:19,683
Fine, let's go.

80
00:05:20,084 --> 00:05:21,085
To The Chicken.

81
00:05:22,520 --> 00:05:23,988
It's called The Kitchen.

82
00:05:25,022 --> 00:05:26,290
Same thing.

83
00:05:27,825 --> 00:05:29,187
When did you get a job there?

84
00:05:29,727 --> 00:05:32,463
It's not like I chose a career.
It's only part-time.

85
00:05:34,899 --> 00:05:35,866
Let's go.

86
00:05:46,944 --> 00:05:48,345
It's so good, isn't it?

87
00:05:48,879 --> 00:05:49,980
Yeah, I guess…

88
00:05:57,087 --> 00:05:58,155
Here we are.

89
00:06:00,858 --> 00:06:04,695
We slowly cooked white asparagus
at a low temperature,

90
00:06:04,695 --> 00:06:07,498
then served it with lemon zest
and cream mousse.

91
00:06:08,199 --> 00:06:10,968
The subtle acidity and soft texture
are the highlights.

92
00:06:14,071 --> 00:06:15,873
What's this sprinkled on top?

93
00:06:16,507 --> 00:06:17,474
Pine nuts.

94
00:06:17,842 --> 00:06:18,843
Crushed nuts.

95
00:06:20,477 --> 00:06:23,314
Crumbles made from roasted pine nuts
and truffle oil,

96
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:25,583
and tomato jelly on the side.

97
00:06:25,583 --> 00:06:28,752
- For the texture and…
- So this is the tomato jelly.

98
00:06:32,122 --> 00:06:35,993
We reduced the gelatin
for texture and flavor.

99
00:06:36,493 --> 00:06:37,561
Try it.

100
00:06:37,561 --> 00:06:39,697
It's so pretty. How can I eat it?

101
00:06:46,103 --> 00:06:48,739
Seriously? You're all hanging out
without me, you traitors!

102
00:06:49,640 --> 00:06:51,208
Who called her?

103
00:06:51,308 --> 00:06:52,810
Like I wouldn't find out?

104
00:06:53,310 --> 00:06:56,547
Mu I, how could you go
to that concert without me?

105
00:06:57,515 --> 00:06:58,649
No, what happened was…

106
00:06:58,916 --> 00:07:02,353
He got me tickets
because I said I like Ian Kim.

107
00:07:02,653 --> 00:07:04,855
Da Hong, if I'd known you liked
Ian Kim…

108
00:07:04,855 --> 00:07:06,857
No, I'm kidding, Yu Il.

109
00:07:07,124 --> 00:07:09,627
Of all the guys in the world,
I only like Mu I.

110
00:07:11,695 --> 00:07:13,631
Hello, Chef. I'm Joo Da Hong.

111
00:07:13,964 --> 00:07:15,265
I know. Nice to meet you.

112
00:07:15,645 --> 00:07:16,901
Min's told me a lot about you.

113
00:07:18,804 --> 00:07:20,638
I wonder what he said about me.

114
00:07:21,305 --> 00:07:22,373
That you're super loud.

115
00:07:24,241 --> 00:07:25,943
I'm glad you already know.

116
00:07:26,443 --> 00:07:30,414
But is it okay for you
to be seen with Min?

117
00:07:31,315 --> 00:07:33,817
It'd be worse if I were seen
with Mu I right now, wouldn't it?

118
00:07:35,374 --> 00:07:37,288
Chef, do you have any stout here?

119
00:07:48,098 --> 00:07:50,067
You should've held back a bit.

120
00:07:50,534 --> 00:07:52,670
Hey, that's easy for you to say.

121
00:07:52,937 --> 00:07:54,772
How could I hold back when I was so mad?

122
00:07:55,139 --> 00:07:57,208
He chewed me out
in front of the whole crew.

123
00:07:57,608 --> 00:07:59,376
- Isn't that right?
- Next to her is Joo Da Hong.

124
00:07:59,376 --> 00:08:01,445
- Yeah, yeah, you're right.
- In front of her, Ryu Min.

125
00:08:01,445 --> 00:08:05,182
- You're right.
- And even this man.

126
00:08:07,017 --> 00:08:09,553
All of this is so surreal.

127
00:08:14,225 --> 00:08:15,226
So annoying.

128
00:08:15,793 --> 00:08:17,094
That director is so weird.

129
00:08:18,395 --> 00:08:19,430
Hey, what is that?

130
00:08:32,343 --> 00:08:35,646
I'm still upset about how you left us
the other day.

131
00:08:36,093 --> 00:08:37,099
If only for my sake,

132
00:08:37,124 --> 00:08:40,080
can't you give Dad just one chance?

133
00:08:44,655 --> 00:08:45,689
Thank you, Chef.

134
00:08:50,528 --> 00:08:52,129
How was the food?

135
00:08:52,630 --> 00:08:55,733
Every dish was so delicious.
Every one of them.

136
00:08:56,700 --> 00:08:59,370
I see why celebrities love this place.

137
00:09:00,137 --> 00:09:01,230
If ever you decide to quit,

138
00:09:01,255 --> 00:09:04,150
you'll hesitate just because
of our staff meals.

139
00:09:04,408 --> 00:09:06,343
You feed the staff here too?

140
00:09:08,312 --> 00:09:10,681
Of course, would we make you work
without feeding you?

141
00:09:12,603 --> 00:09:14,685
I'm excited just thinking about it.

142
00:09:18,103 --> 00:09:19,890
What happened here?

143
00:09:20,991 --> 00:09:23,827
I must've scraped it earlier
while I was taking something out.

144
00:09:25,762 --> 00:09:26,769
Hold on.

145
00:09:32,136 --> 00:09:33,103
Here.

146
00:09:34,104 --> 00:09:35,306
But this is my right hand…

147
00:09:48,018 --> 00:09:49,653
The pattern's a bit much, right?

148
00:09:51,488 --> 00:09:53,490
It's cute, Ms. Pharmacist.

149
00:09:53,891 --> 00:09:54,892
"Ms. Pharmacist?"

150
00:09:57,995 --> 00:09:58,996
I like it.

151
00:10:02,032 --> 00:10:03,033
Hey.

152
00:10:03,100 --> 00:10:06,070
I just found out.
You've never been in a relationship?

153
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:10,808
No comment.

154
00:10:14,612 --> 00:10:16,881
Popular singer Ryu Min,
who's never had a girlfriend.

155
00:10:16,881 --> 00:10:20,417
He was recently rumored to be dating
the pretty and sexy actress Joo Da Hong.

156
00:10:20,918 --> 00:10:21,886
What's it like?

157
00:10:22,620 --> 00:10:24,922
Annoyed? Or excited?

158
00:10:26,323 --> 00:10:27,558
Choose your words wisely.

159
00:10:32,563 --> 00:10:33,631
I was worried about you.

160
00:10:36,901 --> 00:10:39,737
I'm sorry because it's my fault
that this thing happened to you.

161
00:10:41,338 --> 00:10:43,374
I'm okay with people
speaking harshly of me,

162
00:10:45,809 --> 00:10:48,679
but it's hard when my friends and family
suffer because of me.

163
00:10:51,448 --> 00:10:52,650
There's nothing I can do.

164
00:10:54,485 --> 00:10:55,452
Are you okay?

165
00:10:56,487 --> 00:10:57,454
How was it?

166
00:10:58,989 --> 00:11:00,024
How was what?

167
00:11:00,591 --> 00:11:02,793
I had my fill of insults
that were thrown at me.

168
00:11:11,322 --> 00:11:12,503
They were together.

169
00:11:12,937 --> 00:11:14,538
Yu Il, Yu Il. Come, sit.

170
00:11:14,939 --> 00:11:17,675
Chef, stop cooking and sit with us.
We're all full.

171
00:11:18,175 --> 00:11:20,144
- Have a seat.
- Thank you.

172
00:11:29,887 --> 00:11:31,655
Come to think of it, it's kind of odd.

173
00:11:32,089 --> 00:11:33,757
A concert would have lots of people,

174
00:11:34,058 --> 00:11:36,861
and if Yu Il wanted to see it,
you could've just gotten her tickets.

175
00:11:37,995 --> 00:11:38,996
Why did you go together?

176
00:11:39,997 --> 00:11:41,285
Why else would we go together?

177
00:11:42,299 --> 00:11:43,834
I wanted to see it too, so we went.

178
00:11:44,635 --> 00:11:46,070
Still, it's strange.

179
00:11:46,670 --> 00:11:49,039
You went to a concert alone
with a non-celebrity, Mu I?

180
00:11:51,108 --> 00:11:52,376
What do you want to know?

181
00:11:53,377 --> 00:11:56,914
Yu Il, what do you think of Mu I?

182
00:11:57,481 --> 00:11:58,449
As a boyfriend?

183
00:12:00,247 --> 00:12:01,234
What?

184
00:12:02,119 --> 00:12:03,141
What do you mean?

185
00:12:03,471 --> 00:12:05,389
What kind of question is that?

186
00:12:05,689 --> 00:12:07,958
You've never thought about it?

187
00:12:10,628 --> 00:12:13,397
Come on, that's ridiculous.

188
00:12:19,303 --> 00:12:22,173
Even thinking about it again, it's absurd.

189
00:12:24,608 --> 00:12:26,644
Why does it feel like
I've just been dumped?

190
00:12:32,316 --> 00:12:37,288
Mu I, you really are amazing,
and you're great.

191
00:12:39,990 --> 00:12:42,426
But you're really not my type.

192
00:12:48,165 --> 00:12:49,533
Okay, let's hear it.

193
00:12:50,100 --> 00:12:51,468
What kind of man is your type?

194
00:12:54,839 --> 00:12:56,240
An ordinary person?

195
00:12:57,074 --> 00:12:58,075
Be more specific.

196
00:12:59,410 --> 00:13:03,581
Like, I want to come home from work,
have dinner with him,

197
00:13:03,948 --> 00:13:07,418
watch movies and go to
parks together on the weekends,

198
00:13:07,618 --> 00:13:09,553
and then for anniversaries,
use our savings....

199
00:13:09,887 --> 00:13:11,527
to try out restaurants like this one.

200
00:13:11,552 --> 00:13:12,460
Things like that.

201
00:13:19,263 --> 00:13:21,599
We're far from ordinary.

202
00:13:22,032 --> 00:13:23,901
Very far, yeah.

203
00:13:27,571 --> 00:13:28,939
- Thanks so much.
- Sure.

204
00:13:31,075 --> 00:13:32,910
Yu Il, take my car. I'll drive you home.

205
00:13:33,711 --> 00:13:34,745
You're not taking me?

206
00:13:35,179 --> 00:13:36,313
She's my guest.

207
00:13:37,047 --> 00:13:38,115
Well, what about me?

208
00:13:38,115 --> 00:13:39,917
Her house and mine are
on opposite sides of town!

209
00:13:40,217 --> 00:13:42,553
I snuck out, so I need to get back fast.

210
00:13:43,087 --> 00:13:44,655
Should I call you a taxi?

211
00:13:44,855 --> 00:13:47,458
I'm going to go live about this!

212
00:13:48,425 --> 00:13:50,895
I'll be fine. I can take the bus.

213
00:13:51,795 --> 00:13:52,763
I still think…

214
00:13:52,763 --> 00:13:54,699
I'll walk Yu Il home.

215
00:13:54,723 --> 00:13:55,866
She's my employee.

216
00:13:56,066 --> 00:13:57,902
Yeah, that works.

217
00:13:58,636 --> 00:13:59,770
You two look good together.

218
00:14:00,905 --> 00:14:02,006
See you later.

219
00:14:02,673 --> 00:14:05,976
- Take care.
- You too. Bye.

220
00:14:13,984 --> 00:14:18,122
Earlier, I noticed Da Hong
had a lot of questions for you.

221
00:14:19,256 --> 00:14:20,257
I know, right?

222
00:14:21,926 --> 00:14:24,061
Can I ask you something I'm curious about?

223
00:14:26,197 --> 00:14:29,400
How did you get close to Tak Mu I?

224
00:14:32,102 --> 00:14:36,740
My friend is a producer on the show
that Da Hong and Mu I are in.

225
00:14:37,208 --> 00:14:38,809
They said they needed a rooftop,

226
00:14:39,243 --> 00:14:40,511
and I needed the money.

227
00:14:41,545 --> 00:14:42,813
So I rented it out.

228
00:14:44,267 --> 00:14:45,749
I live in a rooftop place.

229
00:14:46,417 --> 00:14:47,418
I see.

230
00:14:48,285 --> 00:14:51,989
But filming in front of your place
doesn't mean everyone gets close.

231
00:14:53,290 --> 00:14:54,959
There was a misunderstanding,

232
00:14:55,326 --> 00:14:58,429
and in the process of clearing it up,
one thing led to another.

233
00:15:00,698 --> 00:15:03,634
What kind of person is Tak Mu I?

234
00:15:06,036 --> 00:15:08,038
At first I didn't think much of him,

235
00:15:08,706 --> 00:15:11,075
but he turned out to be a really good guy.

236
00:15:12,109 --> 00:15:13,368
I can't say for sure,

237
00:15:13,393 --> 00:15:15,355
but one of his MBTI letters
is probably an F.

238
00:15:16,080 --> 00:15:19,950
He's very empathetic and quite sensitive.

239
00:15:21,919 --> 00:15:22,920
What about me?

240
00:15:23,687 --> 00:15:24,855
What do you make of me?

241
00:15:25,990 --> 00:15:28,859
I'm not sure. We've only just met.

242
00:15:30,227 --> 00:15:31,829
We can get to know each other slowly.

243
00:15:33,898 --> 00:15:36,100
Hey, we're here.

244
00:15:37,935 --> 00:15:39,870
How did you know this was my house?

245
00:15:42,673 --> 00:15:43,874
I saw it on your résumé.

246
00:15:43,874 --> 00:15:44,875
(Taewon-ro 17-gil)

247
00:15:49,713 --> 00:15:50,981
- Excuse me, sir.
- Yes?

248
00:15:50,981 --> 00:15:53,117
Drive us to the back,
not the front of the house.

249
00:15:53,117 --> 00:15:54,218
Yes, understood.

250
00:15:54,818 --> 00:15:57,054
- Are you going to climb the wall?
- Yeah.

251
00:15:57,388 --> 00:15:58,856
That's what you get for causing trouble.

252
00:15:59,623 --> 00:16:01,392
Why would you even call that trouble?

253
00:16:03,360 --> 00:16:05,296
- Da Hong.
- Yeah.

254
00:16:05,296 --> 00:16:07,731
What do you think of that chef?

255
00:16:09,466 --> 00:16:10,701
Not that I know exactly,

256
00:16:10,801 --> 00:16:13,103
but Min says
he's from a very wealthy family.

257
00:16:13,571 --> 00:16:14,538
How wealthy?

258
00:16:15,005 --> 00:16:18,742
Super rich. His family members
are all doctors and professors,

259
00:16:19,043 --> 00:16:20,604
but he studied abroad, found cooking,

260
00:16:20,671 --> 00:16:22,646
and became a chef
against his family's wishes.

261
00:16:24,815 --> 00:16:28,352
But what's really amazing is that
he took no help from his family,

262
00:16:28,352 --> 00:16:31,755
started from scratch, opened his place,
and even earned Michelin stars.

263
00:16:33,257 --> 00:16:34,291
That is impressive.

264
00:17:01,719 --> 00:17:02,720
Hope she got home okay.

265
00:17:13,964 --> 00:17:15,933
Man, I don't have her number.

266
00:17:18,402 --> 00:17:19,703
Should I ask Yeon Ju?

267
00:17:22,540 --> 00:17:23,574
It's probably too late.

268
00:17:25,442 --> 00:17:27,711
Da Hong…

269
00:17:29,613 --> 00:17:31,148
She'll ask too many questions.

270
00:17:55,739 --> 00:17:57,908
Did she already quit?

271
00:18:04,582 --> 00:18:07,751
Chef, did you really make
all of these by yourself?

272
00:18:08,586 --> 00:18:09,587
I made them one by one.

273
00:18:10,321 --> 00:18:12,022
Yo, what is going on?

274
00:18:12,122 --> 00:18:14,325
You never cook outside
business hours.

275
00:18:14,859 --> 00:18:17,795
Well, it's just to help
the incoming employee learn the menu.

276
00:18:18,128 --> 00:18:19,630
You've never done that before.

277
00:18:21,398 --> 00:18:22,600
Can you just drop it?

278
00:18:23,634 --> 00:18:25,302
Chef, you're acting strangely.

279
00:18:25,302 --> 00:18:27,037
It's also odd that you're hiring her now.

280
00:18:27,805 --> 00:18:29,874
Was she pretty? Was she sexy?

281
00:18:30,307 --> 00:18:31,375
Dude, seriously?

282
00:18:32,142 --> 00:18:34,211
- Get rid of those, quick.
- Yes, Chef.

283
00:18:38,923 --> 00:18:40,117
I'm hungry.

284
00:18:40,518 --> 00:18:43,521
Of course you are.
You ate nothing all day.

285
00:18:44,355 --> 00:18:47,224
Weirdly, I wasn't during the shoot,
but now that it's over, I am.

286
00:18:47,958 --> 00:18:49,326
Yeong Su, want to eat together?

287
00:18:50,261 --> 00:18:52,463
Sorry, I have to take my mom
to the hospital today.

288
00:18:52,830 --> 00:18:54,331
Right, I forgot.

289
00:18:54,665 --> 00:18:56,233
Want to get something to take home?

290
00:18:56,767 --> 00:18:57,801
No.

291
00:18:58,569 --> 00:19:00,871
I just don't want to eat alone today.

292
00:19:03,107 --> 00:19:05,709
I really don't want to eat alone!

293
00:19:06,277 --> 00:19:09,547
I really, really hate it!
I hate it so much!

294
00:19:09,547 --> 00:19:10,581
Stop it!

295
00:19:16,020 --> 00:19:17,121
- Hey, Yeong Su.
- Yeah?

296
00:19:17,121 --> 00:19:18,088
Drop me off up here.

297
00:19:18,522 --> 00:19:20,457
- Here?
- Yeah, there, there.

298
00:19:21,358 --> 00:19:22,259
Where are you going?

299
00:19:22,359 --> 00:19:26,797
(Gohyang Diner)

300
00:19:28,495 --> 00:19:29,495
Ma'am.

301
00:19:29,900 --> 00:19:31,302
You're not closing now, are you?

302
00:19:31,402 --> 00:19:32,937
Hello, handsome young man.

303
00:19:33,270 --> 00:19:35,506
I just closed up. I'm sorry.

304
00:19:35,639 --> 00:19:39,276
That's too bad.
I haven't eaten anything today.

305
00:19:39,510 --> 00:19:42,924
You may be handsome,
but I just can't cook for you right now.

306
00:19:42,991 --> 00:19:44,381
My rice cooker's broken.

307
00:19:44,582 --> 00:19:45,549
What?

308
00:19:46,202 --> 00:19:48,301
What is so important about work...

309
00:19:48,368 --> 00:19:51,121
that a young man like you would starve
himself all day?

310
00:19:52,022 --> 00:19:54,024
Anyway, come back next time.

311
00:19:54,325 --> 00:19:57,728
Next time, I'll give you big servings,
including today's.

312
00:19:58,195 --> 00:19:59,163
Okay.

313
00:20:02,132 --> 00:20:03,367
Let me help you.

314
00:20:09,039 --> 00:20:10,007
Here you go.

315
00:20:10,274 --> 00:20:12,610
What's this?
You came with the pretty one?

316
00:20:12,710 --> 00:20:14,478
Hey! It's Gong Yu Il!

317
00:20:15,346 --> 00:20:16,580
Hey, what a surprise.

318
00:20:17,982 --> 00:20:19,316
What on earth?

319
00:20:19,316 --> 00:20:22,753
You yourself are starving,
and you let this one starve too?

320
00:20:24,154 --> 00:20:26,190
It's not like that. We came separately.

321
00:20:26,590 --> 00:20:29,059
Take her and get her some food quickly.

322
00:20:29,059 --> 00:20:31,896
How could you starve
this skin-and-bones student?

323
00:20:32,530 --> 00:20:34,732
I've told you several times
I'm not a student…

324
00:20:34,965 --> 00:20:38,169
Okay, okay. I won't call you
a student anymore. Bye.

325
00:20:38,736 --> 00:20:40,157
- Goodbye.
- Take care.

326
00:20:40,224 --> 00:20:41,224
All right.

327
00:20:43,207 --> 00:20:44,341
Did you get home okay yesterday?

328
00:20:44,575 --> 00:20:47,912
Yes, Chef Kang took me right to
my front door.

329
00:20:49,180 --> 00:20:50,581
Did you quit the convenience store?

330
00:20:52,016 --> 00:20:53,617
Yes, it ended up that way.

331
00:20:55,686 --> 00:20:56,987
When do you start at The Kitchen?

332
00:20:58,122 --> 00:20:59,089
From next week.

333
00:21:00,124 --> 00:21:01,158
I see.

334
00:21:02,526 --> 00:21:05,496
That's all I wanted to know.
Let's go eat.

335
00:21:06,330 --> 00:21:08,799
- What?
- She told me to take the student to eat.

336
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:10,434
Let's go, student.

337
00:21:12,069 --> 00:21:13,337
Where are we going?

338
00:21:13,637 --> 00:21:15,472
You said you'd treat me after the concert.

339
00:21:16,073 --> 00:21:18,442
That dinner at The Kitchen
doesn't count, does it?

340
00:21:19,476 --> 00:21:21,536
You can buy me the dinner.
The one you promised.

341
00:21:24,748 --> 00:21:26,817
Here's the caprese with pansies.

342
00:21:26,984 --> 00:21:30,454
Cut the burrata open,
and eat it with the tomatoes.

343
00:21:30,454 --> 00:21:31,488
Enjoy.

344
00:21:32,423 --> 00:21:33,424
Thank you.

345
00:21:44,935 --> 00:21:46,103
We'll go with Course A.

346
00:21:46,203 --> 00:21:47,905
Sure, we'll bring it out to you soon.

347
00:21:50,674 --> 00:21:52,877
(Cornflower Lemon Mango Mousse, $170)

348
00:21:53,911 --> 00:21:56,580
$170 times two is $340.

349
00:21:56,814 --> 00:21:58,916
At the minimum wage of $10 an hour,

350
00:21:59,316 --> 00:22:02,319
that's about 32.9 hours?

351
00:22:03,454 --> 00:22:05,422
(Gong Yu Il's Bankbook)

352
00:22:12,396 --> 00:22:14,020
- Are you not eating?
- Sorry?

353
00:22:15,799 --> 00:22:17,101
No, I am.

354
00:22:20,371 --> 00:22:21,472
Are you uneasy about something?

355
00:22:23,841 --> 00:22:24,808
No.

356
00:22:26,777 --> 00:22:30,414
Hey, what if people get the wrong idea?

357
00:22:32,283 --> 00:22:33,284
Don't worry.

358
00:22:33,784 --> 00:22:36,787
To others, we'll just look like
a couple on a date.

359
00:22:37,254 --> 00:22:38,289
That's what I mean.

360
00:22:39,023 --> 00:22:41,692
That's why I'm self-conscious.

361
00:22:43,227 --> 00:22:44,195
Look around us.

362
00:22:45,262 --> 00:22:49,867
Everyone's busy taking pictures and eating
expensive food. They don't even see me.

363
00:22:50,668 --> 00:22:53,771
So since we're here, let's enjoy it.

364
00:22:54,672 --> 00:22:56,240
I want to enjoy it,

365
00:22:56,874 --> 00:22:59,443
but it's so pretty I can't dig in.

366
00:23:04,515 --> 00:23:08,586
Today's last course is a lemon mango
mousse sprinkled with cornflowers.

367
00:23:08,752 --> 00:23:10,354
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.

368
00:23:14,925 --> 00:23:17,728
It's another pretty flower garden.

369
00:23:26,036 --> 00:23:27,104
This is so good.

370
00:23:28,506 --> 00:23:30,741
My mouth's been blessed for a second day.

371
00:23:32,510 --> 00:23:33,570
So cute.

372
00:23:37,553 --> 00:23:38,554
What?

373
00:23:41,385 --> 00:23:44,355
I mean… the way you eat reminds me
of Yeong Su.

374
00:23:45,689 --> 00:23:48,492
He's really cute when he eats.

375
00:24:04,842 --> 00:24:06,744
When did you pay?

376
00:24:07,077 --> 00:24:08,779
Earlier, when you went to the restroom.

377
00:24:09,914 --> 00:24:10,948
Why did you do that?

378
00:24:11,448 --> 00:24:13,584
I'm just grateful that you ate
with me.

379
00:24:14,185 --> 00:24:16,787
I really didn't want to eat alone today.

380
00:24:17,755 --> 00:24:20,224
But I was the one who said I'd pay.

381
00:24:20,824 --> 00:24:22,121
Pay next time.

382
00:24:22,445 --> 00:24:23,919
That way, we can meet again.

383
00:24:26,096 --> 00:24:27,431
Shall we walk for a bit?

384
00:24:32,536 --> 00:24:33,938
Who are they to each other?

385
00:24:33,938 --> 00:24:36,507
- Tak Mu I looks so much better in person.
- Right?

386
00:24:36,874 --> 00:24:38,742
Joo Da Hong might get upset about it.

387
00:24:38,742 --> 00:24:41,412
- I know. What's going on?
- What's wrong with Tak Mu I?

388
00:24:41,645 --> 00:24:44,181
- Turned out well, right?
- Yeah, Tak is very handsome.

389
00:24:44,181 --> 00:24:45,282
I took it secretly.

390
00:24:46,684 --> 00:24:49,887
No matter how I think about it,
I should've paid.

391
00:24:50,321 --> 00:24:54,325
You lent me the book for free.
You could've charged me a high fee.

392
00:24:54,792 --> 00:24:57,061
Well, you took me to the concert
for the book.

393
00:24:57,461 --> 00:24:59,763
No, I got the better end of the deal.

394
00:25:00,698 --> 00:25:03,400
Once I start working again,
let's go back there.

395
00:25:03,801 --> 00:25:06,670
Though I don't know if we'll still
be able to meet by then.

396
00:25:08,105 --> 00:25:10,040
That stings a little.

397
00:25:12,992 --> 00:25:14,078
I didn't mean to…

398
00:25:14,178 --> 00:25:15,513
Hey, give me your number.

399
00:25:17,348 --> 00:25:19,216
I still don't have your number.

400
00:25:20,284 --> 00:25:21,385
That's true.

401
00:25:21,719 --> 00:25:23,988
Even for the concert,
you came to my house to get me.

402
00:25:24,522 --> 00:25:25,523
Can you put it in?

403
00:25:45,242 --> 00:25:46,277
By the way,

404
00:25:46,944 --> 00:25:49,480
I read Book 3, and I thought about it.

405
00:25:50,247 --> 00:25:53,050
I'm not worried about Half Moon,
who's now living in the forest.

406
00:25:53,450 --> 00:25:55,085
Now, I'm more worried about Star.

407
00:25:56,820 --> 00:25:57,788
Why?

408
00:25:58,622 --> 00:26:02,826
The day Half Moon left, Star's dad
also announced he was leaving home.

409
00:26:04,595 --> 00:26:05,629
Did he?

410
00:26:07,064 --> 00:26:08,866
Do you think he really left?

411
00:26:16,974 --> 00:26:18,576
This is really good. Try some.

412
00:26:19,743 --> 00:26:21,478
Want to come over for ramyeon?

413
00:26:35,826 --> 00:26:37,361
I have lost my mind. I've lost it.

414
00:26:38,262 --> 00:26:41,765
What do I do about the mess at the house
and the awkwardness between us?

415
00:26:48,205 --> 00:26:50,274
I really don't have to eat ramyeon here.

416
00:26:51,442 --> 00:26:54,645
You know what?
Just wait here for five minutes.

417
00:27:09,793 --> 00:27:12,530
It feels different being here
at her invitation.

418
00:27:14,031 --> 00:27:15,966
Okay, you can come in now.

419
00:27:34,552 --> 00:27:36,020
I'm in trouble.

420
00:27:36,487 --> 00:27:38,622
I'll need to run for at least three hours.

421
00:27:38,856 --> 00:27:40,491
How are you so good at cooking ramyeon?

422
00:27:40,691 --> 00:27:41,892
I almost added rice too.

423
00:27:42,660 --> 00:27:45,796
When was the last time you had ramyeon?

424
00:27:48,499 --> 00:27:49,600
I don't even remember.

425
00:27:50,401 --> 00:27:51,632
When I was little,

426
00:27:51,952 --> 00:27:54,414
I got in trouble for eating it
behind my grandma's back.

427
00:27:55,239 --> 00:27:58,142
I don't know if you know,

428
00:27:58,776 --> 00:28:01,345
but I was raised by my grandma
after my parents passed away.

429
00:28:02,379 --> 00:28:04,748
You know my grandma is an actress, right?

430
00:28:05,583 --> 00:28:07,985
Of course, how could I not?

431
00:28:08,285 --> 00:28:09,687
She's very famous.

432
00:28:10,955 --> 00:28:15,492
But how did you get started
in the acting business, Mu I?

433
00:28:16,026 --> 00:28:17,219
Because of your grandmother?

434
00:28:18,689 --> 00:28:19,830
Because of her?

435
00:28:21,565 --> 00:28:22,700
I guess that's true.

436
00:28:23,868 --> 00:28:27,171
After my parents died, I went to set
with my grandma,

437
00:28:27,304 --> 00:28:30,641
and the child actor bailed,
so I was cast on the spot.

438
00:28:32,009 --> 00:28:33,210
Really?

439
00:28:33,878 --> 00:28:35,145
Sure, it was all pretend.

440
00:28:35,746 --> 00:28:36,914
But there was a mom,

441
00:28:37,348 --> 00:28:38,516
a dad,

442
00:28:39,250 --> 00:28:40,484
and older and younger siblings.

443
00:28:42,119 --> 00:28:44,522
Maybe I just enjoyed
that bustling atmosphere

444
00:28:45,256 --> 00:28:46,991
because I kept thinking about it for days.

445
00:28:48,559 --> 00:28:51,061
So I begged her to let me act.

446
00:28:52,062 --> 00:28:53,998
Did your grandma allow it?

447
00:28:54,098 --> 00:28:55,499
Yes. Surprising, right?

448
00:28:59,136 --> 00:29:02,106
We were all acting, but I could say
"Mom" and "Dad" as much as I wanted.

449
00:29:12,516 --> 00:29:13,484
Are you crying?

450
00:29:14,518 --> 00:29:16,587
No, who's crying…

451
00:29:20,391 --> 00:29:22,793
- I should do the dishes.
- No, I'll do it.

452
00:29:23,527 --> 00:29:24,962
You're a guest…

453
00:29:25,095 --> 00:29:26,163
You should go home now.

454
00:29:26,664 --> 00:29:28,226
Then let's make a bet.

455
00:29:28,251 --> 00:29:29,226
A dishwashing bet.

456
00:29:30,668 --> 00:29:31,669
A bet?

457
00:29:35,639 --> 00:29:36,974
I can't resist a bet.

458
00:29:39,810 --> 00:29:41,078
How about a word chain game?

459
00:29:42,379 --> 00:29:44,281
- Muzak!
- What?

460
00:29:44,415 --> 00:29:45,983
You said word chain. Muzak!

461
00:29:46,884 --> 00:29:47,852
Ak?

462
00:29:50,321 --> 00:29:51,322
Actinouranium.

463
00:29:53,290 --> 00:29:54,325
Acti…

464
00:29:57,027 --> 00:29:59,029
Five. Four.

465
00:29:59,430 --> 00:30:00,798
- Three.
- Wait!

466
00:30:00,798 --> 00:30:02,967
Two, one. Time's up!

467
00:30:05,202 --> 00:30:06,237
Let's go one more time.

468
00:30:06,871 --> 00:30:08,839
I'll start. Monster!

469
00:30:11,041 --> 00:30:12,076
Stereo.

470
00:30:12,142 --> 00:30:13,210
Stereo?

471
00:30:13,277 --> 00:30:14,378
Daybreak!

472
00:30:15,446 --> 00:30:16,714
Populism!

473
00:30:20,017 --> 00:30:22,753
Why isn't she picking up?

474
00:30:23,554 --> 00:30:25,489
She said she was done for the day
hours ago.

475
00:30:26,790 --> 00:30:27,958
Did she fall asleep?

476
00:30:28,092 --> 00:30:29,894
The person you are trying to reach…

477
00:30:36,700 --> 00:30:39,170
You actually wanted me
to do the dishes, didn't you?

478
00:30:39,904 --> 00:30:41,272
No, it's really not that.

479
00:30:41,805 --> 00:30:44,241
I just really like bets,

480
00:30:44,742 --> 00:30:46,710
and I have a pretty good vocabulary.

481
00:30:53,484 --> 00:30:54,585
What are you staring at?

482
00:30:56,353 --> 00:30:57,421
Well…

483
00:30:57,755 --> 00:31:00,057
I know this room won't be on the show,

484
00:31:00,057 --> 00:31:02,393
but according to the story,
the female lead lives here.

485
00:31:02,793 --> 00:31:06,130
But with you washing dishes
in front of me like this,

486
00:31:06,530 --> 00:31:08,999
it feels like I've stepped into the story
within the show.

487
00:31:09,333 --> 00:31:11,602
I think it's pretty amazing.

488
00:31:13,137 --> 00:31:14,471
This is amazing to you, is it?

489
00:31:15,940 --> 00:31:18,943
But are you really a Ryu Min fan?

490
00:31:20,578 --> 00:31:22,146
What? Why?

491
00:31:22,746 --> 00:31:25,950
Typically, fans would
never use merch like this.

492
00:31:29,453 --> 00:31:32,636
I didn't have any cups
I could use one day,

493
00:31:32,661 --> 00:31:34,483
so I just used it for a sec…

494
00:31:35,993 --> 00:31:37,761
But there are so many cups here.

495
00:31:41,398 --> 00:31:45,169
Actually, I'm not.
It's my friend who is Min's fan.

496
00:31:45,736 --> 00:31:47,538
If I display his merchandise like that,

497
00:31:47,538 --> 00:31:50,207
she said Ryu Min would like it
when he saw it.

498
00:31:50,875 --> 00:31:52,710
Well, then why…

499
00:31:53,644 --> 00:31:56,714
At the time, you adamantly accused me
of being a stalker…

500
00:32:02,386 --> 00:32:03,420
Kkong!

501
00:32:03,587 --> 00:32:05,356
Hey, Gong Yu Il, open the door!

502
00:32:07,491 --> 00:32:08,592
What do we do?

503
00:32:09,627 --> 00:32:11,529
- So what?
- Hey, Kkong Kkong!

504
00:32:11,562 --> 00:32:13,931
What if she brings up
something about the book?

505
00:32:13,931 --> 00:32:14,899
That can't happen.

506
00:32:14,899 --> 00:32:16,066
Hide. Hurry!

507
00:32:16,767 --> 00:32:17,768
Kkong Kkong!

508
00:32:17,768 --> 00:32:19,703
The closet over there!

509
00:32:19,870 --> 00:32:21,105
Hurry!

510
00:32:21,105 --> 00:32:22,473
Coming.

511
00:32:26,610 --> 00:32:27,878
Yeah, coming!

512
00:32:27,878 --> 00:32:29,280
Okay.

513
00:32:34,919 --> 00:32:36,053
What's this?

514
00:32:37,388 --> 00:32:39,323
You don't look like you just washed up.

515
00:32:39,990 --> 00:32:42,226
I, I was in the bathroom, bathroom.

516
00:32:42,226 --> 00:32:43,627
Were you doing number two?

517
00:32:43,627 --> 00:32:45,262
You didn't pick up any of my calls.

518
00:32:45,796 --> 00:32:48,666
It was on vibrate,
so I must not have heard.

519
00:32:50,067 --> 00:32:51,101
Did you eat ramyeon?

520
00:32:52,670 --> 00:32:53,838
Yeah, I did.

521
00:32:55,406 --> 00:32:56,807
Well, that's weird.

522
00:32:57,141 --> 00:33:01,212
Two bowls, two pairs of chopsticks,
and two spoons.

523
00:33:02,079 --> 00:33:02,980
So…

524
00:33:03,647 --> 00:33:05,749
I was washing this morning's dishes too.

525
00:33:06,951 --> 00:33:10,988
But you couldn't have eaten
two packages at once.

526
00:33:11,488 --> 00:33:12,823
You had ramyeon for two meals?

527
00:33:13,257 --> 00:33:14,258
Yeah.

528
00:33:14,258 --> 00:33:15,492
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

529
00:33:17,328 --> 00:33:18,762
Hey, where are you going?

530
00:33:18,762 --> 00:33:20,331
Why are you going in there?

531
00:33:20,397 --> 00:33:22,666
You were with Yong Seok, weren't you?

532
00:33:22,967 --> 00:33:23,934
No, I wasn't!

533
00:33:24,358 --> 00:33:26,170
Don't you lie to me.

534
00:33:26,170 --> 00:33:28,239
This punk is going to get it.
Hey, come out!

535
00:33:28,772 --> 00:33:30,207
What are you doing?

536
00:33:30,207 --> 00:33:31,942
- Why are you doing this?
- Let go.

537
00:33:32,676 --> 00:33:33,811
Come on!

538
00:33:34,645 --> 00:33:35,980
He's in there.

539
00:33:35,980 --> 00:33:36,981
Move.

540
00:33:37,248 --> 00:33:39,183
What, why?

541
00:33:39,350 --> 00:33:40,317
Move aside.

542
00:33:40,317 --> 00:33:42,052
It's just my closet.

543
00:33:42,119 --> 00:33:43,454
It's not just a closet.

544
00:33:43,854 --> 00:33:45,022
Stop it, please.

545
00:33:46,657 --> 00:33:47,691
Stop!

546
00:33:50,327 --> 00:33:52,163
Hey, Kim Yong Seok!

547
00:33:52,363 --> 00:33:53,330
Come out!

548
00:33:53,430 --> 00:33:55,399
Yeon Ju, it's not what you think…

549
00:33:58,135 --> 00:33:59,870
My leg's asleep!

550
00:34:02,173 --> 00:34:03,340
My leg's asleep!

551
00:34:03,340 --> 00:34:04,708
Tak Mu I!

552
00:34:23,861 --> 00:34:27,965
So I lent him the book
and he was grateful for it.

553
00:34:28,899 --> 00:34:31,969
But if he's the one grateful,
why did you cook for him?

554
00:34:33,003 --> 00:34:36,140
Because I lent him that book,
he took me to the Ian Kim concert,

555
00:34:36,140 --> 00:34:37,875
and I couldn't afford to buy him dinner.

556
00:34:39,276 --> 00:34:41,212
I don't know, it's a long story.

557
00:34:42,252 --> 00:34:43,547
You even went to a concert?

558
00:34:44,381 --> 00:34:47,184
I'm saying this out of nosy concern,

559
00:34:47,184 --> 00:34:50,754
but you know celebrities and we
are completely different species, right?

560
00:34:52,156 --> 00:34:54,391
How are they different?
They're all people.

561
00:34:54,491 --> 00:34:55,459
Listen to yourself.

562
00:34:55,459 --> 00:34:57,928
You remember, right?
When I dated that new actor?

563
00:34:58,596 --> 00:35:01,232
How could I forget?
You made such a fuss about it.

564
00:35:01,532 --> 00:35:05,069
I couldn't go anywhere or do anything.

565
00:35:05,069 --> 00:35:07,338
It felt even worse than not being able

566
00:35:07,338 --> 00:35:09,940
to call my father "Father," okay?

567
00:35:10,007 --> 00:35:13,244
Foodie tours, holding hands while walking,
shopping, that kind of stuff.

568
00:35:13,344 --> 00:35:17,114
Even though I craved all
the ordinary things everyone else does,

569
00:35:17,114 --> 00:35:20,017
I endured all of it. Then his career
took off and he dumped me.

570
00:35:20,618 --> 00:35:23,687
And that was with a newbie,
so when you're with a top star?

571
00:35:24,688 --> 00:35:27,291
That coffee incident was nothing.

572
00:35:27,791 --> 00:35:30,794
You'd either get stabbed with a knife
or die of a broken heart.

573
00:35:31,061 --> 00:35:32,763
I'd say it'll be one of the two.

574
00:35:33,998 --> 00:35:35,432
Who said we're dating?

575
00:35:35,666 --> 00:35:36,634
No.

576
00:35:37,101 --> 00:35:39,370
I'm saying don't get involved at all.

577
00:35:39,370 --> 00:35:41,639
That'll never happen, ever.

578
00:35:41,839 --> 00:35:42,806
Never!

579
00:35:49,914 --> 00:35:53,551
("Rooftop Romance")

580
00:36:00,257 --> 00:36:02,092
We demand an explanation
from those involved.

581
00:36:03,666 --> 00:36:04,668
What is this?

582
00:36:10,034 --> 00:36:11,001
Is anyone there?

583
00:36:13,871 --> 00:36:15,239
Somebody, get me out!

584
00:36:20,010 --> 00:36:22,079
Hello! Hello!

585
00:36:22,379 --> 00:36:24,181
Hey, somebody get me out!

586
00:36:24,949 --> 00:36:27,451
Somebody get me out! Get me out!

587
00:36:45,636 --> 00:36:47,538
Pick up the phone, Tak Mu I.

588
00:36:47,872 --> 00:36:49,240
Did you already call?

589
00:36:49,240 --> 00:36:51,008
Yeah, but he's not answering.

590
00:36:51,242 --> 00:36:53,177
Yeong Su, you know who it is, right?

591
00:36:53,477 --> 00:36:55,246
It’s way too early for this chaos.

592
00:36:55,446 --> 00:36:56,680
Don't you do this to me.

593
00:36:56,981 --> 00:36:58,382
It's a woman, a woman!

594
00:36:58,382 --> 00:37:00,951
Not even me! Another woman!

595
00:37:01,051 --> 00:37:03,921
- I've arrived at Mu I's place.
- Tell me who as soon as you know!

596
00:37:07,458 --> 00:37:10,528
Hey, did you eat with some woman alone?

597
00:37:11,095 --> 00:37:12,296
What are you talking about?

598
00:37:12,563 --> 00:37:13,631
You don't know?

599
00:37:13,898 --> 00:37:15,766
Look at this.

600
00:37:16,233 --> 00:37:19,336
(I saw Tak Mu I at a restaurant today)

601
00:37:26,500 --> 00:37:27,912
This is so frustrating.

602
00:37:28,379 --> 00:37:30,014
(He was eating with some woman,
and they looked cozy together.)

603
00:37:32,106 --> 00:37:34,084
And he said no one would care.

604
00:37:38,856 --> 00:37:40,624
About this mystery woman,

605
00:37:40,624 --> 00:37:42,426
check if her personal info got leaked.

606
00:37:43,928 --> 00:37:46,030
Nope, I read all the comments. Nothing.

607
00:37:48,098 --> 00:37:49,567
This woman's profile…

608
00:37:50,534 --> 00:37:52,369
Why does she look so familiar?

609
00:37:55,206 --> 00:37:57,808
But that Tak Mu I, though,

610
00:37:58,609 --> 00:38:00,177
no wonder women like him.

611
00:38:00,578 --> 00:38:04,081
That innocent-looking face
with a hint of sexiness, you know?

612
00:38:05,316 --> 00:38:07,484
Wait a minute.
He goes to your salon, doesn't he?

613
00:38:07,484 --> 00:38:08,519
Yeah.

614
00:38:08,519 --> 00:38:10,554
Well, some friends of mine told me

615
00:38:10,554 --> 00:38:12,790
that the hair and makeup teams both say

616
00:38:12,790 --> 00:38:14,225
he's super kind and nice.

617
00:38:14,658 --> 00:38:16,460
He never throws his weight around,

618
00:38:16,485 --> 00:38:18,696
and even brings his drinks in a tumbler.

619
00:38:18,721 --> 00:38:20,597
Because he feels bad asking for drinks.

620
00:38:22,533 --> 00:38:24,401
Why do you look so pleased?

621
00:38:25,903 --> 00:38:27,037
I forgot to tell you…

622
00:38:27,271 --> 00:38:29,640
I quit the convenience store
and found a new part-time job.

623
00:38:31,108 --> 00:38:32,776
Yeon Ju already told me.

624
00:38:33,811 --> 00:38:36,814
Instead of a job,
how about marrying into money?

625
00:38:38,015 --> 00:38:39,383
Why would you say that?

626
00:38:40,818 --> 00:38:42,019
When I was working part-time,

627
00:38:42,019 --> 00:38:44,889
I went to The Kitchen every payday
to see that chef.

628
00:38:44,889 --> 00:38:46,090
Why? Is he good-looking?

629
00:38:46,323 --> 00:38:47,358
Girl.

630
00:38:48,659 --> 00:38:49,627
He's so hot.

631
00:38:50,961 --> 00:38:54,999
He's a bit different from Tak Mu I,
like a different kind of sexy, you know?

632
00:38:55,299 --> 00:38:56,600
There's something about him.

633
00:38:57,835 --> 00:38:59,203
Is he sexy?

634
00:39:22,893 --> 00:39:24,595
You still won't tell me who it is?

635
00:39:24,795 --> 00:39:25,796
No.

636
00:39:26,096 --> 00:39:28,899
If I tell you, it'll reach Da Hong's ears,
obviously.

637
00:39:29,166 --> 00:39:30,380
I don't want to deal with her.

638
00:39:30,404 --> 00:39:31,635
I get it.

639
00:39:32,970 --> 00:39:34,805
So what will you do
about your lack of sleep?

640
00:39:35,272 --> 00:39:37,141
I'm still having the same dream.

641
00:39:37,808 --> 00:39:40,044
Someone's forcing food down my throat,

642
00:39:40,778 --> 00:39:43,314
or I'm stuck in a tight space,
and can't move.

643
00:39:43,781 --> 00:39:45,182
How do you feel in the dream?

644
00:39:46,917 --> 00:39:49,987
Well, scared,

645
00:39:50,955 --> 00:39:53,724
lonely, and suffocated.

646
00:39:54,425 --> 00:39:56,126
You wouldn't want counseling from me.

647
00:39:56,360 --> 00:39:58,099
Do you want me to find you
a good therapist?

648
00:39:58,513 --> 00:39:59,729
I'll be fine.

649
00:40:00,231 --> 00:40:01,799
It's not bad enough for counseling.

650
00:40:02,700 --> 00:40:04,168
Just prescribe me some sleeping pills.

651
00:40:05,336 --> 00:40:07,505
I tried to tough it out somehow,

652
00:40:08,305 --> 00:40:11,141
but I can't
because it might affect filming.

653
00:40:11,909 --> 00:40:13,511
I can do that,

654
00:40:13,878 --> 00:40:15,846
but we should find the underlying cause.

655
00:40:16,847 --> 00:40:17,815
Yeah, I know.

656
00:40:25,189 --> 00:40:26,156
Yes, Chef.

657
00:40:26,790 --> 00:40:29,260
You haven't forgotten your first day
tonight, right?

658
00:40:29,894 --> 00:40:30,928
Of course not.

659
00:40:30,928 --> 00:40:33,430
Is there anything I should bring
separately?

660
00:40:33,898 --> 00:40:37,067
No, just come as you are.
Your uniform is all ready too.

661
00:40:37,468 --> 00:40:39,403
Okay, I won't be late.

662
00:40:39,837 --> 00:40:40,838
See you later.

663
00:40:41,038 --> 00:40:42,039
Okay.

664
00:40:49,780 --> 00:40:52,082
You're Mr. Tak, right?

665
00:40:54,618 --> 00:40:56,187
It is you, Tak Mu I!

666
00:40:57,888 --> 00:40:59,390
I get that a lot.

667
00:40:59,390 --> 00:41:03,160
Come on, as if I wouldn't recognize
the face of my "son-in-law."

668
00:41:03,661 --> 00:41:06,330
My daughter is a huge fan of Tak Mu I.

669
00:41:07,231 --> 00:41:08,966
Not long ago, my "son-in-law,"

670
00:41:08,966 --> 00:41:11,569
you had that movie "I Didn't Know Then."

671
00:41:12,102 --> 00:41:15,539
And now you're on that "Rooftop…"
whatchamacallit?

672
00:41:16,040 --> 00:41:17,575
You're doing that drama show.

673
00:41:18,876 --> 00:41:20,477
- Yes.
- My goodness.

674
00:41:21,312 --> 00:41:23,214
You're more handsome in person.

675
00:41:24,682 --> 00:41:25,749
Thank you.

676
00:41:27,852 --> 00:41:30,721
But who are you actually dating?

677
00:41:31,522 --> 00:41:35,292
Is it Joo Da Hong, or the woman
in the photo the other day?

678
00:41:37,242 --> 00:41:39,430
Every time there's a dating
rumor about my "son-in-law,"

679
00:41:40,030 --> 00:41:42,566
my daughter goes completely nuts.

680
00:41:45,169 --> 00:41:48,005
That woman and I aren't like that at all.

681
00:41:50,774 --> 00:41:53,244
Look, could I get an autograph later?

682
00:41:54,211 --> 00:41:55,813
A photo would be even better, okay?

683
00:42:07,258 --> 00:42:08,359
Excuse me, sir.

684
00:42:09,994 --> 00:42:11,028
I'm sorry, but…

685
00:42:53,337 --> 00:42:55,372
(Mu I)

686
00:42:55,372 --> 00:42:57,641
The person you are trying to reach is not…

687
00:43:03,147 --> 00:43:05,216
I'll prescribe a mild sleeping pill
for now.

688
00:43:05,516 --> 00:43:08,285
Don't drink alcohol, and take it only
when you really can't sleep.

689
00:43:08,412 --> 00:43:11,064
The person you are trying to
reach is not available...

690
00:43:15,893 --> 00:43:18,596
Why does your voice sound like that?
Is something wrong?

691
00:43:20,197 --> 00:43:21,232
Yu Il…

692
00:43:23,234 --> 00:43:24,802
I don't have a mask to cover my face,

693
00:43:27,471 --> 00:43:28,739
and I'm really dizzy.

694
00:43:30,174 --> 00:43:34,044
Could you come get me?

695
00:43:40,050 --> 00:43:41,285
There you are!

696
00:43:41,852 --> 00:43:43,587
- Hey, you scared me.
- Are you okay?

697
00:43:43,721 --> 00:43:46,023
- Yes.
- You should've called for an ambulance.

698
00:43:46,123 --> 00:43:48,959
The thing is… this has happened before,

699
00:43:49,727 --> 00:43:52,229
and the media speculated
that I was on drugs.

700
00:43:53,097 --> 00:43:56,400
So I had to go to the police station
for a drug test,

701
00:43:57,334 --> 00:44:00,571
Anyway, it's a lot of hassle.

702
00:44:02,339 --> 00:44:03,607
Yeah, but still…

703
00:44:06,143 --> 00:44:10,214
I want to get home
without people noticing me…

704
00:44:15,352 --> 00:44:16,387
Just a moment.

705
00:44:19,557 --> 00:44:20,724
Put this on, and we'll go.

706
00:44:21,492 --> 00:44:23,561
I think this will stand out more.

707
00:44:23,928 --> 00:44:28,265
But they'll see a chicken head,
not your face, so it'll be okay, right?

708
00:44:28,265 --> 00:44:29,266
Let's get moving.

709
00:44:33,137 --> 00:44:34,371
- Careful.
- Welcome.

710
00:44:40,377 --> 00:44:41,712
- Are you okay?
- No.

711
00:44:46,562 --> 00:44:48,018
Are you going to some event?

712
00:44:49,053 --> 00:44:50,120
Yes.

713
00:44:57,494 --> 00:44:58,696
Just a moment.

714
00:45:00,030 --> 00:45:02,299
Got it. Hang in there a bit longer.

715
00:45:14,551 --> 00:45:15,635
Thank you.

716
00:45:16,380 --> 00:45:18,516
Are you sure you don't need
to go to a hospital?

717
00:45:18,883 --> 00:45:19,917
Yes.

718
00:45:20,484 --> 00:45:22,253
It's because I haven't been sleeping.

719
00:45:24,855 --> 00:45:26,724
Okay, get some rest.

720
00:45:33,964 --> 00:45:36,467
I'm going to Mu I's
to give him some side dishes.

721
00:45:36,467 --> 00:45:37,768
I'm almost there.

722
00:45:37,768 --> 00:45:38,836
He said he's off today.

723
00:45:39,036 --> 00:45:41,539
Tell him to consider
getting serious with Da Hong.

724
00:45:42,806 --> 00:45:44,041
Okay.

725
00:45:44,041 --> 00:45:46,343
I'll do my best to tell him, Grandma.

726
00:45:53,551 --> 00:45:54,585
Hey.

727
00:45:54,852 --> 00:45:56,387
He was wearing a strange mask,

728
00:45:56,387 --> 00:45:59,123
and he went in with some woman
thirty minutes ago.

729
00:46:00,724 --> 00:46:01,725
Yeah.

730
00:46:04,862 --> 00:46:08,732
("Rooftop Romance")

731
00:46:18,209 --> 00:46:19,410
(Restrain Emotions)

732
00:46:25,502 --> 00:46:27,651
He works really hard.

733
00:46:33,224 --> 00:46:34,225
Hey.

734
00:46:36,360 --> 00:46:39,063
Yu Il, what brings you here?

735
00:46:40,498 --> 00:46:44,101
He called, saying he was out on the street
and asked if I could come get him…

736
00:46:44,735 --> 00:46:47,571
He called you too.

737
00:46:48,038 --> 00:46:49,240
Is Mu I okay?

738
00:46:49,840 --> 00:46:51,475
He fell asleep a little while ago.

739
00:46:52,309 --> 00:46:54,211
Take a seat. Please.

740
00:46:59,583 --> 00:47:00,618
Are you okay?

741
00:47:02,820 --> 00:47:05,289
I was worried because there were
so many missed calls.

742
00:47:05,456 --> 00:47:08,092
I got dizzy and felt like throwing up,

743
00:47:08,526 --> 00:47:10,261
but I'm okay because Yu Il helped me.

744
00:47:10,995 --> 00:47:13,464
Thank goodness for her.
Mu I, let's go to the hospital first.

745
00:47:13,464 --> 00:47:15,733
I feel better now that I've slept.

746
00:47:16,167 --> 00:47:19,170
Yeong Su, can you take Yu Il home?

747
00:47:20,004 --> 00:47:22,273
Okay. Sleep a bit more, yeah?

748
00:47:22,573 --> 00:47:24,041
I will. Thanks.

749
00:47:32,416 --> 00:47:34,185
What? Where did she go?

750
00:47:37,821 --> 00:47:38,889
What's this?

751
00:47:41,792 --> 00:47:44,428
I have to go to work. I'll see myself out.

752
00:48:15,693 --> 00:48:16,794
It looks good on you.

753
00:48:17,428 --> 00:48:18,562
Thank you.

754
00:48:19,463 --> 00:48:23,067
Hello, I'm Gong Yu Il.
I look forward to working with you all.

755
00:48:23,267 --> 00:48:24,335
Welcome.

756
00:48:29,073 --> 00:48:30,107
We're glad you're here.

757
00:48:54,265 --> 00:48:55,566
You got a lot on your mind?

758
00:48:58,602 --> 00:48:59,603
Hey, sis.

759
00:48:59,970 --> 00:49:03,541
Do you know anything about
the author of "Star and the Half Moon?"

760
00:49:06,838 --> 00:49:07,946
Well, let's see.

761
00:49:08,013 --> 00:49:09,680
I think I heard somewhere before...

762
00:49:09,680 --> 00:49:12,516
that a high school girl wrote it.

763
00:49:13,551 --> 00:49:14,518
Really?

764
00:49:18,322 --> 00:49:21,258
By the way, when is Auntie coming back?

765
00:49:21,759 --> 00:49:24,261
Her daughter's postpartum care should
only take two weeks.

766
00:49:25,930 --> 00:49:26,931
You would think so.

767
00:49:27,464 --> 00:49:29,200
I miss Auntie's cooking.

768
00:49:30,434 --> 00:49:31,969
You're really stubborn, you know.

769
00:49:32,203 --> 00:49:33,871
You could just find someone else.

770
00:49:34,905 --> 00:49:36,336
I don't like finding new people.

771
00:49:37,871 --> 00:49:40,110
Ms. Kim does good work.

772
00:49:43,347 --> 00:49:45,950
By the way,
why don't you have a boyfriend?

773
00:49:49,053 --> 00:49:53,023
Let's not ask each other
about dating, Mu I.

774
00:49:54,458 --> 00:49:55,426
Eat.

775
00:50:05,636 --> 00:50:06,770
I'm exhausted.

776
00:50:08,372 --> 00:50:09,740
My legs.

777
00:50:10,774 --> 00:50:13,511
Higher-paying jobs
pay better for a reason.

778
00:50:20,518 --> 00:50:22,653
Are you sure you don't need
to go to a hospital?

779
00:50:22,987 --> 00:50:23,988
Yes.

780
00:50:24,622 --> 00:50:26,257
It's because I haven't been sleeping.

781
00:50:31,028 --> 00:50:34,165
How long has he gone without sleep
to end up like that?

782
00:50:44,475 --> 00:50:46,143
(Author Kkong Kkong's Draft Notebook)

783
00:50:46,143 --> 00:50:47,444
(It'll be hard to post for a while.)

784
00:50:47,444 --> 00:50:48,779
(Could this be the author?)

785
00:50:52,917 --> 00:50:54,118
Could it be…

786
00:51:00,891 --> 00:51:03,861
How do I make a close male friend
see me as more than a friend?

787
00:51:04,695 --> 00:51:05,729
Are you talking about Mu I?

788
00:51:06,330 --> 00:51:07,631
Why do you even bother asking?

789
00:51:09,733 --> 00:51:11,502
Considering his personality,

790
00:51:11,502 --> 00:51:13,904
going suddenly from a close friend
to that special someone...

791
00:51:13,904 --> 00:51:15,139
doesn't seem possible.

792
00:51:15,472 --> 00:51:17,141
No, no, it's happened before.

793
00:51:18,409 --> 00:51:21,045
Mu I used to date a woman
who was once a close friend.

794
00:51:21,679 --> 00:51:23,113
- Really?
- Yeah.

795
00:51:23,547 --> 00:51:25,182
She was a friend of mine too.

796
00:51:25,182 --> 00:51:26,483
I figured if she knew I knew,

797
00:51:26,483 --> 00:51:28,485
I figured they’d ditch me,
so I played dumb.

798
00:51:29,987 --> 00:51:31,856
That's a lot of restraint for
Joo Da Hong.

799
00:51:32,656 --> 00:51:34,491
I thought, just wait till I turn legal,

800
00:51:34,491 --> 00:51:36,760
the day I'm no longer a minor,
I'll snatch him away.

801
00:51:37,294 --> 00:51:38,262
Or so I thought…

802
00:51:38,929 --> 00:51:39,897
But?

803
00:51:40,498 --> 00:51:41,499
They broke up.

804
00:51:44,034 --> 00:51:45,069
I see.

805
00:51:47,805 --> 00:51:51,208
But are you really serious about
Mu I?

806
00:51:51,909 --> 00:51:52,877
Not kidding around?

807
00:51:54,144 --> 00:51:55,913
Of course not.

808
00:51:56,714 --> 00:51:59,416
I've never even thought about anyone else.

809
00:51:59,583 --> 00:52:00,718
Not for a single moment.

810
00:52:19,036 --> 00:52:20,104
(Mettoogi)

811
00:52:20,104 --> 00:52:23,574
(Unfortunately, we will not
be moving forward with your application.)

812
00:52:27,811 --> 00:52:29,980
Well, they made their decision quickly…

813
00:52:35,519 --> 00:52:37,288
Should I try writing again?

814
00:52:42,326 --> 00:52:45,596
(Cast Holding)

815
00:52:45,596 --> 00:52:49,934
My dear, dear Kkong must be
feeling terrible inside.

816
00:52:50,668 --> 00:52:51,769
Producer Yeon Ju!

817
00:52:51,769 --> 00:52:53,704
Yes. Hello!

818
00:52:53,704 --> 00:52:55,139
I'm getting close to Yu Il.

819
00:52:55,606 --> 00:52:57,241
Is that right?

820
00:52:57,675 --> 00:53:00,611
Our friend Yu Il's hanging out
with celebrities a lot lately.

821
00:53:01,545 --> 00:53:03,681
She's so nice, really.

822
00:53:04,348 --> 00:53:05,950
What was Yu Il like as a student?

823
00:53:06,183 --> 00:53:10,421
Well, she was mostly quiet,
but she was famous.

824
00:53:10,855 --> 00:53:11,889
She was famous?

825
00:53:11,889 --> 00:53:15,159
Yes, she is very talented at writing.

826
00:53:15,159 --> 00:53:17,361
She swept every award there was,

827
00:53:17,361 --> 00:53:19,530
and when she wrote novels,
the whole class passed them around.

828
00:53:20,423 --> 00:53:22,099
That's so cool.

829
00:53:23,698 --> 00:53:25,436
Don't tell her I said that.

830
00:53:25,569 --> 00:53:26,570
She hates it.

831
00:53:27,838 --> 00:53:29,507
- Take care.
- Okay.

832
00:53:36,514 --> 00:53:38,816
So, where did you get that?
It hasn't even been published.

833
00:53:39,283 --> 00:53:40,851
Why should I tell you?

834
00:53:40,885 --> 00:53:42,989
It wasn't an official publication,

835
00:53:43,013 --> 00:53:44,455
just a few proofreading copies printed.

836
00:53:44,655 --> 00:53:47,725
I saw the book discarded
at the recycling area, so I took it home.

837
00:53:49,126 --> 00:53:50,094
Kkong!

838
00:53:50,094 --> 00:53:51,061
(Congrats on the grand prize, Kkong Kkong)

839
00:53:51,061 --> 00:53:55,065
There must be a reason the author
didn't put it out into the world.

840
00:53:55,065 --> 00:53:56,300
Maybe it's embarrassing.

841
00:54:17,054 --> 00:54:18,088
No, no.

842
00:54:18,289 --> 00:54:20,858
I really don't have the money…

843
00:54:24,829 --> 00:54:25,863
You're coming home now?

844
00:54:29,012 --> 00:54:30,013
I'm sorry.

845
00:54:31,435 --> 00:54:32,736
I said I'm sorry, okay?

846
00:54:34,205 --> 00:54:35,806
I did the unforgivable, all right?

847
00:54:36,407 --> 00:54:38,843
So let's get back together.

848
00:54:39,009 --> 00:54:41,178
You broke up with me
by sending one text message,

849
00:54:41,178 --> 00:54:42,446
so what's this about now?

850
00:54:42,780 --> 00:54:44,415
There's no one like you, okay?

851
00:54:44,415 --> 00:54:45,850
Girls at work only see the stats.

852
00:54:47,117 --> 00:54:48,786
You said you found someone.

853
00:54:49,620 --> 00:54:50,654
That girl?

854
00:54:50,921 --> 00:54:53,190
Don't even bring her up...

855
00:54:53,424 --> 00:54:56,026
We flirted at work,
then we met outside the office.

856
00:54:56,026 --> 00:54:58,829
Suddenly she said she doesn't want
to date someone from work.

857
00:54:59,163 --> 00:55:01,599
I mean, she said she liked me
because I had cute hands.

858
00:55:01,765 --> 00:55:04,635
Why are you telling me this?
Beg her to take you back.

859
00:55:04,935 --> 00:55:07,071
You really think I haven't tried?

860
00:55:07,071 --> 00:55:09,964
I went to her house and got on my knees.
But still...

861
00:55:11,041 --> 00:55:12,610
she was already dating
a superior at work.

862
00:55:13,010 --> 00:55:14,745
The son of a politician.

863
00:55:15,546 --> 00:55:17,715
The thing is, it turns out
she's a total snob.

864
00:55:17,882 --> 00:55:19,283
I didn't want to hear any of that.

865
00:55:20,251 --> 00:55:22,686
Deal with your heartbreak on your own.

866
00:55:24,722 --> 00:55:26,423
Let's get back together.

867
00:55:26,657 --> 00:55:28,125
Let's be completely honest.

868
00:55:28,125 --> 00:55:30,761
I'm at a much better place
in life than you, aren't I?

869
00:55:31,295 --> 00:55:32,930
I'm saying I'll even help you get a job.

870
00:55:34,798 --> 00:55:35,833
What?

871
00:55:37,368 --> 00:55:38,335
Get lost.

872
00:55:39,236 --> 00:55:40,271
Come on.

873
00:55:40,838 --> 00:55:42,540
She said get lost, you idiot!

874
00:55:45,543 --> 00:55:48,012
Do I have to say it again?
Get lost, idiot!

875
00:55:48,679 --> 00:55:50,614
It's all lies, from what I hear.

876
00:55:51,015 --> 00:55:52,049
Get out of our faces!

877
00:55:53,751 --> 00:55:54,919
Let's go.

878
00:55:55,219 --> 00:55:56,453
Go!

879
00:56:03,994 --> 00:56:05,029
Cheers!

880
00:56:05,095 --> 00:56:06,096
Nice.

881
00:56:10,433 --> 00:56:11,437
Nice!

882
00:56:14,171 --> 00:56:17,141
You've learned so many of my secrets.

883
00:56:18,142 --> 00:56:19,910
I didn't mean to listen.

884
00:56:20,845 --> 00:56:24,381
It's fine. I really wanted a drink today,

885
00:56:25,149 --> 00:56:26,784
and now I even get a free beer.

886
00:56:28,586 --> 00:56:30,921
But seriously, why are you here tonight?

887
00:56:31,088 --> 00:56:32,156
There's no shoot, right?

888
00:56:34,091 --> 00:56:38,629
I came to figure out how to make
the man I like like me back.

889
00:56:39,330 --> 00:56:42,032
Since there's no one in particular
I can ask, I thought I'd ask you.

890
00:56:45,936 --> 00:56:48,506
You mean Tak Mu I, right?

891
00:56:48,672 --> 00:56:49,707
Yeah.

892
00:56:50,007 --> 00:56:51,842
I planned on waiting patiently,

893
00:56:52,276 --> 00:56:55,946
but he is out eating alone
with some woman,

894
00:56:55,946 --> 00:56:57,014
so I got anxious.

895
00:56:59,416 --> 00:57:03,721
You saw me. I don't have it all together
when it comes to dating.

896
00:57:05,089 --> 00:57:08,559
And I'm sure it's nothing serious
between them.

897
00:57:17,268 --> 00:57:18,302
What is it?

898
00:57:18,502 --> 00:57:20,871
Bathroom. I just drank beer.

899
00:57:30,414 --> 00:57:32,149
So much has happened.

900
00:57:43,694 --> 00:57:46,030
What brings you here?

901
00:57:46,931 --> 00:57:49,066
I'm giving you now what I couldn't
give you then.

902
00:57:49,834 --> 00:57:51,569
Author Kkong Kkong.

903
00:58:10,068 --> 00:58:12,615
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
